schema: spec-driven

context: |
  {{ project_name }}: {{ project_description }}
  Repository process and safety constraints live in AGENTS.md and applicable module-level AGENTS.md files.
  Project-specific engineering rules live in docs/engineering/project-rules.md.
  OpenSpec is the planning contract for non-trivial product and architecture work.
  openspec/specs describes accepted current behavior; an active openspec/changes delta describes the approved change to that behavior.
  Reuse existing domain models, source-of-truth ownership, integrations and repository conventions unless a change explicitly replaces them.
  A non-trivial OpenSpec change is complete only after project checks, semantic OpenSpec verification, recorded PASS evidence and method, archive, and configured publication.

rules:
  proposal:
    - State goals and non-goals explicitly.
    - Identify affected existing domains, integrations, contracts and source-of-truth ownership.
    - Prefer evolving the existing system over creating parallel canonical sources.
  design:
    - Document migration/backfill, compatibility, audit/history, rollback/cutover and performance implications when relevant.
    - Resolve shared contracts before declaring workstreams safe to run in parallel.
  tasks:
    - Express dependencies and mark only genuinely independent work as parallelizable.
    - Define logical commit boundaries for non-trivial work.
    - Include targeted tests, regression checks and end-to-end acceptance scenarios.

operations:
  apply:
    guidance:
      - Follow AGENTS.md for the configured workflow profile, GitHub synchronization, check selection and publication safety.
      - No silent divergence: update proposal/specs/design/tasks before knowingly implementing changed intent, behavior, technical approach or execution dependencies.
      - Mark a task complete only after implementation and required verification for that task.
  archive:
    guidance:
      - Preserve durable architecture/runbook information in docs/ when it is operational context rather than product behavior.
      - Confirm task checkboxes and verification reflect implemented state before archive.
      - For non-trivial changes, require project-specific checks/QA and semantic OpenSpec verification before archive.
      - Prefer /opsx:verify when available; otherwise document the equivalent completeness/correctness/coherence review.
      - After material findings are resolved, record `OpenSpec-Verify: PASS` and `Verification-Method: <method>` in the active change verification.md.
      - Use `python3 scripts/openspec_lifecycle.py archive <change>` as the normal project archive entrypoint so completion requirements are mechanically checked.
